message.content:
Below is a minimal example of an **interactive rotating card** using only HTML and CSS.  
When you hover over the card, it rotates 180° around its Y‑axis (you can change the axis or angle if you wish).

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* Container that holds the card */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D effect */
  width: 300px;
  height: 200px;
  margin: 50px auto;
}

/* The card itself */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff9a9e 0%, #fad0c4 100%);
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  transition: transform .6s ease;   /* Smooth rotation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;     /* Needed for 3D transforms */
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* Hover effect – rotate 180° around Y‑axis */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* Optional: content inside the card */
.card-content {
  position: relative;
  width: 100%;
  height: 100%;
  backface-visibility: hidden;    /* Hide backside while rotating */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
  color: #fff;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  text-align: center;
  padding: 20px;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-content">
      <p>Przykładowy tekst na karcie.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Sets the 3D perspective so the rotation looks realistic. |
| `.card` | The actual card element. `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps child elements in 3D space. |
| `.card:hover` | Applies a 180° rotation on the Y‑axis when the mouse hovers over the card. |
| `.card-content` | Holds the visible content. `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the backside during rotation. |

Feel free to adjust colors, dimensions, or the rotation axis (`rotateX`, `rotateZ`) to fit your design.
